From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
Date: Sun, 14 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] uwsgi: restore deprecation-warning suppression

Up to 2025.2 the carried patch disable-python-deprecation-warnings-wsgi
added

    SetEnv PYTHONWARNINGS "ignore"

to the eight mod_wsgi vhost templates OSISM deploys behind Apache
(aodh, cloudkitty, gnocchi, heat x2, keystone, masakari, zun), gated on
kolla_disable_python_deprecation_warnings.

2026.1 migrates those services from mod_wsgi to uWSGI and deletes every
wsgi-<service>.conf.j2 the patch edited, so the patch was correctly
dropped from patches/2026.1 -- but nothing took its place. The services
still run Python; only the Apache layer that carried the setting is
gone. osism/defaults all/099-kolla.yml still sets

    kolla_disable_python_deprecation_warnings: "yes"

and on 2026.1 nothing reads it, so deprecation warnings are back in
those services' logs while the flag reads as still effective. Found by
kolla_retired_patch_orphan in osism/release.

Restore the behaviour at the layer that replaced mod_wsgi. All uWSGI
services share one template, service-uwsgi-config/templates/uwsgi.ini.j2,
so the one hunk here replaces the eight the old patch carried, and the
gate variable and its semantics are unchanged -- an operator who set the
flag keeps the behaviour across the upgrade without touching anything.

The scope widens as a side effect: the shared template backs 22 roles at
2026.1 (aodh, barbican, blazar, cinder, cloudkitty, cyborg, designate,
glance, gnocchi, heat, horizon, ironic, keystone, magnum, manila,
masakari, mistral, neutron, nova, octavia, placement, trove) rather than
the original eight. That is the flag doing what its name says; all seven
services from the old set that still exist at 2026.1 are covered (zun
was removed upstream).

env= is uWSGI's own mechanism for the worker environment, applied before
the application is loaded, which is what PYTHONWARNINGS needs. There is
no non-patch route: 2026.1 exposes no per-service extra-environment
variable and uwsgi.ini.j2 has no env hook.

Signed-off-by: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
---
 .../roles/service-uwsgi-config/templates/uwsgi.ini.j2  | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ansible/roles/service-uwsgi-config/templates/uwsgi.ini.j2 b/ansible/roles/service-uwsgi-config/templates/uwsgi.ini.j2
index e8873eefc..096a00dbe 100644
--- a/ansible/roles/service-uwsgi-config/templates/uwsgi.ini.j2
+++ b/ansible/roles/service-uwsgi-config/templates/uwsgi.ini.j2
@@ -6,6 +6,9 @@ chunked-input-limit = {{ service_uwsgi_config_chunked_input_limit }}
 {% endif %}
 die-on-term = true
 enable-threads = true
+{% if kolla_disable_python_deprecation_warnings | default(false) | bool %}
+env = PYTHONWARNINGS=ignore
+{% endif %}
 exit-on-reload = false
 hook-master-start = unix_signal:15 gracefully_kill_them_all
 {% if service_uwsgi_config_tls_backend | bool %}
